                <pb facs="0230" n="130" sameAs="frus:frus1884/pg130"/>

                <head>No. 81.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Morton to Mr. Frelinghuysen.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-12-28"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 28,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The withdrawal of the decrees of 27th November, which will be published
                    to-morrow, limits the time for the admission of American pork products to the
                    20th January at the ports of Havre, Bordeaux, and Marseilles instead of
                    Nantes.</p>
                <p>Telegram of yesterday received this morning.</p>
                <closer><signed>MORTON.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
